- 2026-09-26, S2 of the specification rung (`reviews/spec-refused-examples-judgement.md`, the Fable judgement): "S2 yes, take the verdicts for rung S". Rung S, now in batch 5, revises each refused example to the one library's shape:
  - the where-clause section's empty list becomes `object Empty[\T\] extends List[\T\]`;
  - the covariance example becomes the library's widening function with bounded static parameters;
  - "a subtrait of every instantiation" stays as the counterexample that introduces the rule;
  - `convenience.tex`'s `Nothing` becomes `Nothing[\T\]`, with no `excludes`, and the exception chapters' defaults become `Nothing[\String\]` and `Nothing[\Exception\]`;
  - `Object` (and `Tuple`, whose prose leans on it) loses the algebraic supertraits, with `===` an operator on `Any`;
  - the internal appendix gets one sentence at each of its three passages;
  - each original is kept in the text as "Not allowed", the specification's own form (`basic/traits.tex:286-292`);
  - the rule is stated once, in Luchangco's two-part form under "instantiation exclusion": which instantiations exclude each other in `basic/types-vals-vars.tex`, the rule on declarations in `basic/traits.tex`;
  - the 2012 `covariant` keyword goes into the decision record.
  Asked the same hour whether the keyword is future work or on the critical path, he was told it is future work: no library declaration and no microGPT line uses it. It comes as two ledger entries among the S2 items: a defect row (the checker accepts it, the compiled run crashes, walk refuses) and worklist item 12 reworded to declaration-site variance by the keywords. Still open from the judgement's section 11, one per message:
  - the tower chapters' sequencing with the flattening rung;
  - whether sizes and boolean arguments count in the rule;
  - row 331 re-gated on static-argument inference;
  - worklist item 12;
  - `RationalQuantity`;
  - whether the keyword is mentioned in the text (default: record only);
  - the five candidate ledger rows;
  - what S1's citations call the unrevised copy.
  `CLIMB-BATCH-4.md`'s option (b) is corrected when S is briefed.

